&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Utility Plant accruals were $23,349 and $51,158&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;at&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;December 31,&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;and 2024, respectively. Gross additions to Utility Plant (less nuclear fuel) on the Statement of Cash Flows excludes $23,349 and $51,158 as of December 31,&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;and 2024, respectively, of significant non-cash transactions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;The composite depreciation rate is&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;0.8&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;% and&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;0.7&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;%&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;at&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;December 31,&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;and 2024 respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;7.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Risk Management&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -18pt; padding-left: 18pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Credit Risk&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; -aw-import: spaces;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Our principal customers for natural gas transportation services are exploration and production companies conducting business on the outer continental shelf of the Gulf of Mexico. We have concentrations of receivables from these customers throughout this&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;region. These concentrations of customers may affect our overall credit risk in that risk factors can negatively affect the credit quality of the entire sector. Where exposed to credit risk, we analyze the customers&amp;#8217; financial condition prior to entering into an agreement, establish credit limits and monitor the appropriateness of those limits on an ongoing basis. We also obtain parental guarantees, cash deposits or letters of credit from customers to provide credit support, where appropriate, based on our financial analysis of the customer and the regulatory or contractual terms and conditions applicable to each contract.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-bottom: 0pt; margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; text-indent: -18pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;8.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;Mississippi Canyon's pro forma tax expense is reflected in its Statement of Income as tax expense and the related current and deferred tax liabilities (or assets) are reflected on its Comparative Balance Sheet. As the member is responsible for the taxes related to Mississippi Canyon. In 2023 and post years income taxes are accrued in accordance with the FERC Policy Statement on Income Tax Allowance permitting the accrual of income taxes on a pass-through entity and the associated taxes accrued are treated as deemed contributions from the owners, whereas net operating loss carryovers are treated as deemed distributions. The deemed contribution recorded was $980,272 in 2025 and $915,098 in 2024 and was included within Other Paid-In Capital on the Comparative Balance Sheet.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;In 2018 pursuant to guidance established in FERC Docket No. PL19-2-000, we began amortizing the regulatory asset utilizing the Reverse South Georgia flowback methodology over the remaining regulatory life of the assets. The remaining regulatory life of the public utility property held in the plant account is determined through FERC approved depreciation rates and, as of December 31, 2018, was near the end of this pre-determined useful life. In accordance with the&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;aforementioned FERC&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;guidance, the amortization of the excess and/or deficient ADIT is recorded to Other Regulatory Assets/Liabilities (Account 182/254) with off-setting entries to provision for deferred income taxes (Account 410.1 or 411.1). As of December 31,&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;2025&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;&amp;#160;the remaining regulatory asset related to excess and/or deficient ADIT was fully amortized.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 50.95pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-indent: -50.95pt; padding-left: 31pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;The following table reflects the components of the provision for income taxes for the period ended:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman'; font-weight: bold;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse;" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td style="border-top-style: solid; border-top-width: 1pt; border-bottom-style: solid; border-bottom-width: 1pt; padding: 1.5pt 1.25pt; vertical-align: bottom;" colspan="8"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Provision (Benefit) for Income Taxes (U.S. dollars)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td style="border-top-style: solid; border-top-width: 1pt; padding-right: 1.25pt; padding-left: 1.25pt; padding-bottom: 0.25pt; vertical-align: middle;"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: 'Times New Roman';"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td style="border-top-style: solid; border-top-width: 1pt; padding: 1.5pt 1.25pt 1.75pt; vertical-align: bottom;" colspan="7"&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: center; font-size: 12pt;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold;"&gt;Years Ended December 31,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
